 "_doc": "Gotham as the console maps it, after Eliot R. Brown's canon map (No Man's Land, 1999): three islands — Uptown, Midtown, Downtown — split by the Sprang and Finger rivers; the mainland across the Gotham River, with Wayne Manor out in Gotham County over the Robert Kane Memorial Bridge; Arkham on its island in the river; Tricorner and Blackgate offshore; Blüdhaven a short ride up the coast (its neighbourhoods from the Nightwing comics). The Narrows, Burnside and the East End come from later canon. Coordinates are 0–100 on a stylised map, north up. 'match' lists other ways people name a place; 'kind' is district or landmark.",
